# Anthropic API rules for this project

## Model IDs. Use these exact strings.
- claude-sonnet-5 for the conversational intake agent
- claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 for cheap mechanical calls
- claude-opus-5 exists but is not needed in this project

Never replace these with claude-3-5-sonnet, claude-3-opus, claude-sonnet-4, or any other
older identifier. If a model string looks unfamiliar to you, it is still correct. Leave it.

## Hard constraints on claude-sonnet-5
- Never set temperature, top_p, or top_k. Any non-default value returns a 400 error.
- Adaptive thinking is on by default. Do not try to enable it.
- There is no manual thinking budget parameter. To turn thinking off for a fast call,
  pass thinking: { type: "disabled" }.
- Always set an explicit max_tokens on every request.

## API basics
- REST endpoint: https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
- Required headers for raw curl: x-api-key, anthropic-version: 2023-06-01, content-type: application/json
- TypeScript SDK package: @anthropic-ai/sdk
- The SDK reads the key from the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable automatically.
  Never pass the key as a string literal in code.

## Structured outputs
Constrained JSON uses a top level output_config parameter on messages.create:

output_config: { format: { type: "json_schema", schema: { ... } } }

Rules for the schema:
- Every object must set additionalProperties: false
- Keep optional fields to a minimum. Each optional field grows the compiled grammar.
- This is not the same as tool use and it is not response_format. Do not convert it to either.

## Security rules, no exceptions
- The Anthropic key is server side only.
- Never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
- Never call the Anthropic API from a client component or from browser code.
- Never write the key into any committed file.
